# SHAD0W

SHAD0W is a deterministic quantitative research laboratory. Its central question is whether a precisely specified market hypothesis produces a reproducible, executable, risk-adjusted edge after realistic costs.

P0.0 established the repository operating foundation. P0.1 established typed, provider-neutral market-data contracts with UTC availability semantics, deterministic validation, provenance, canonical SHA-256 dataset identity, and local synthetic fixtures. P0.2A established a small deterministic close-price feature kernel: simple returns, strict full-window population rolling statistics and z-scores, semantic warm-up/unavailability states, and availability propagation. P0.2B is complete without additional code: the initial condition is expressible by thresholding the existing z-score. P0.3 adds one deterministic, provider-neutral, signal-only mean-reversion hypothesis. P0.4A establishes chronological event ordering and strict future-opportunity eligibility: a completed-bar signal cannot use that bar's close. P0.4B adds one authoritative, per-instrument, price-free lifecycle with pending actions and simulated position state. It has no fill prices, quantities, risk authorization, costs, P&L, or broker integration. P0.4C is next: the narrow task of composing market, feature, strategy, timeline, and lifecycle evidence into a chronological simulation run.

## Development

The project supports Python 3.12 and newer. [`uv`](https://docs.astral.sh/uv/) is the preferred local environment manager.

```powershell
uv sync --group dev
uv run pytest
uv run ruff check .
uv run ruff format --check .
uv run mypy src tests
```

The checks cover contract behavior, not research or trading profitability. See [data contracts](docs/DATA_CONTRACTS.md), [the roadmap](docs/PROJECT_STRATEGY_AND_ENGINEERING_ROADMAP.md), [architecture](docs/ARCHITECTURE.md), and [research method](docs/RESEARCH_METHOD.md).

